<article class="env-lemma" id="04KN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04KN">Lemma <span data-tag="04KN">10.43.3</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. If $R$ is geometrically reduced over $k$, and $S \subset R$ is a multiplicative subset, then the localization $S^{-1}R$ is geometrically reduced over $k$. If $R$ is geometrically reduced over $k$, then $R[x]$ is geometrically reduced over $k$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. Hints: A localization of a reduced ring is reduced, and localization commutes with tensor products. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>